dialect protocol
protocol stdio.jpg.diff
version 1
schema stdio.jpg
start record

# P2-FG2: REAL binary diff frame, replacing F6's `print_diff().into_bytes()` text-as-binary
# shortcut (`../../🦀️component.rs`'s old `DiffCodec::encode_diff` -- per the P2-W0 census, 100% of
# stdio's `DiffCodec` impls were still on this shortcut). `format u8` + `flags u16le` (bit `i`,
# LSB first, marks the field at declaration position `i` present -- `JpgDiff` has SIXTEEN
# independently-optional top-level fields, `width`=0 .. `other-segments`=15, hence a `u16`
# bitmask rather than xml's `u8`/json's single bool) as two REAL fixed fields, individually
# protocol-walked.
#
# Past that header, the (up to 16) present fields' own payloads are bundled into ONE opaque
# trailing `bytes` chain rather than sixteen separately-declared conditional fields: this dialect's
# `Cond` (`if flags eq N`) can only test a field's WHOLE value against a literal, not an individual
# BIT of it (no bitwise-AND primitive exists, `📖️grammar-recipe.md` §2.2's own `Cond` section), so
# a per-bit-guarded field list isn't expressible here even before considering that several of
# jpg's own diff payloads (`quant-tables`/`huffman-tables`/`other-segments`'s id/index-keyed
# collection triples, `frame`'s `JpgFrameChange` enum) independently hit the SAME
# `protocol-array-of-records`/`protocol-prim-ref-recursion` mechanism gaps every other stdio
# artifact's diff/mutation payload hits (`📖️grammar-recipe.md` §5) -- once ANY field of this frame
# is structurally unwalkable, bundling every field's payload into the SAME opaque tail, instead of
# partially structuring only the simplest ones, is the honest, minimal-surface choice: the Rust
# `encode_diff`/`decode_diff` side (`../../🦀️component.rs`'s `§ValueBinaryCodecs`/
# `§DiffValueBinaryCodecs` regions) stays genuinely, fully structured (bit-tested, individually
# typed, real varint/fixed-width fields, real collection-triple counts) and round-trip tested
# independently -- this protocol file's opaque tail is a DESCRIPTION-layer boundary only.
framing record
header fixed 3
field format u8
field flags u16
chain payload bytes
